note arrpart (OM-2, spec 6): `part A o k` as argument pi of function f (index + 1); md 57 / 58 when `view` /
note `edit` was written before it. A is a name (a global is error 19, a fresh array 27); o, then k, are
note ulong values. Checks, in this order: o <= len A (CMP Xo, Xlen; B.HI trap 3), then k <= len A - o (SUB,
note CMP, B.HI trap 3); the wrapped o + k is never formed. The part is a view of A + o * size with count k:
note an edit when A is writable (local or edit) and no `view` was written, else a view. It goes only to an
note unsized parameter (error 7). Out as arrarg; rt is A, so for error 19 the part counts as its base.
fn arrpart f ulong pi ulong md ulong to void
p = add mul sub f 1 6 pi
e = arrname
i = sub e 1
k = ulong get nm_kind i
if ge k 6
fail 7
end
if eq k 4
fail 19
end
fz_arg e
if eq get fn_pk p 3
if eq md 57
fail 20
end
if and ne k 1 ne k 3
fail 20
end
else
if eq md 58
fail 7
end
end
if ne ulong get nm_type i ulong get fn_pt p
fail 7
end
if ne get fn_pl p 0
fail 7
end
rdval 0 5 255 0
if ne get rt 0 5
fail 7
end
ro = matreg get rk 0 get rv 0 5
rdval 0 5 255 0
if ne get rt 0 5
fail 7
end
rn = matreg get rk 0 get rv 0 5
d = partck i ro rn
ux = add mul get depth 0 6 pi
put ul_k ux 1
put ul_v ux rn
put rt 0 e
put rk 0 5
put rv 0 d
end
